  "editorial_md": "### Intuition\nReversing swaps the first character with the last, the second with the second-to-last, and so on until the two ends meet.\n\n### Algorithm\nKeep two indices, `i` at the start and `j` at the end. While `i < j`, swap `s[i]` and `s[j]`, then move both inward.\n\n```python\ndef reverseString(s):\n    i, j = 0, len(s) - 1\n    while i < j:\n        s[i], s[j] = s[j], s[i]\n        i += 1\n        j -= 1\n    return s\n```\n\n### Complexity\nO(n) time and O(1) extra space — each pair is swapped exactly once, in place.",
